[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Duplicate element TAG is a third silent grammar collision

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-DUPLICATE-ELEMENT-TAG-SILENT
TITLE: Duplicate element TAG is a third silent grammar collision
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Measured on 0.28.3. Two grammar elements sharing a TAG parse clean and export
exit 0. DocumentGrammar registers each element with an assignment into
elements_by_type keyed on the tag, so the lookup keeps the LAST while
grammar.elements still holds both. Verified directly: a two-element grammar with
both elements tagged X reports elements X and X, registered_elements holding the
single name X, and elements_by_type for X carrying the SECOND element's fields.

That is the same class as the duplicate field title and duplicate relation role
cases the implementation brief records, and the same direction as the field one.
The brief says those two are the only checks that belong at Nix evaluation; that
count is one short.

packages/strictdoc-grammar/lib/emit.nix already guards it in its whole-file
renderer alongside the other two. The open item is the brief's line, and the
prior question of whether such checks belong to the emitter at all or to the
type surface.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Found while proving the emitter, by asking whether the two documented collisions
were the whole set rather than by happening to hit one.
<<<
